.TH ORG-TOOLS.TOML 5 "2026-11-08" "org-tools" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
org-tools.toml \- configuration file for the org command-line suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I .org-tools.toml
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B .org-tools.toml
file configures formatting rules, lint diagnostics, agenda warning windows, workflow keywords, roam directories, and capture templates for
.BR org (1).
Configuration files use TOML syntax.
All settings are optional and fall back to Emacs Org-mode compatible defaults when omitted.
.SH CONFIGURATION HIERARCHY
.BR org (1)
resolves configuration settings in the following precedence order:
.IP 1. 4
Explicit file path passed via the
.B \-\-config
command-line flag.
.IP 2. 4
File path specified in the
.B ORG_TOOLS_CONFIG
environment variable.
.IP 3. 4
Nearest
.I .org-tools.toml
file discovered in the current working directory or any parent directory.
.IP 4. 4
User configuration file at
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml .
.IP 5. 4
Built-in Emacs Org-mode compatible default values.
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [format]
Controls auto-fixable formatting rules (`F001` through `F008`):
.TP
.B trailing_whitespace \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Remove trailing spaces and tabs from non-protected lines (`F001`).
.TP
.B blank_lines \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Collapse consecutive blank lines to `max_consecutive_blank_lines` (`F002`).
.TP
.B max_consecutive_blank_lines \fR(integer, default: \fB1\fR)
Maximum consecutive blank lines permitted when `blank_lines` is enabled.
.TP
.B heading_blank_lines \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Enforce blank lines before headings (`F003`).
.TP
.B heading_blank_lines_before \fR(integer, default: \fB1\fR)
Number of blank lines inserted before headings when `heading_blank_lines` is enabled.
.TP
.B table_format \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Align Org pipe table columns and normalize separator rows (`F004`).
.TP
.B property_drawer_align \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Align property values inside `:PROPERTIES:` drawers (`F005`).
.SS [lint]
Controls structural and stylistic lint rules (`E001` through `I007`):
.TP
.B disabled_rules \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Rule identifiers or kebab-case names to skip during `org fmt check` (for example, `["W001", "heading-level-gap"]`).
.TP
.B id_scope \fR(string, default: \fB"workspace"\fR)
Resolution boundary for `:ID:` uniqueness checks and cross-file link validation (`"file"`, `"workspace"`, or `"vault"`).
.SS [landscapes.<slug>]
Defines composable project clusters, member repositories, and forge globs:
.TP
.B description \fR(string, optional)
Human-readable summary of the landscape scope.
.TP
.B projects \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Member project slugs belonging to this landscape.
.TP
.B forges \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Repository forge path or glob patterns belonging to this landscape (alias: `forge_prefixes`).
.TP
.B includes \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Slugs of child landscapes recursively included by this landscape.
.SS [agenda]
Controls daily and weekly agenda timeline projection:
.TP
.B deadline_warning_days \fR(integer, default: \fB14\fR)
Lead-time warning window in days for `DEADLINE:` timestamps without an explicit `-Nd` warning suffix.
.SS [todo]
Defines workspace-wide TODO state sequences when files omit `#+TODO:` keywords:
.TP
.B active \fR(array of strings, default: \fB["TODO", "NEXT", "WAITING"]\fR)
Incomplete workflow keywords representing active tasks.
.TP
.B done \fR(array of strings, default: \fB["DONE", "CANCELLED"]\fR)
Terminal workflow keywords representing completed tasks.
.SS [roam]
Configures `org-roam` v2 note discovery and daily note paths:
.TP
.B directory \fR(string, default: \fB"."\fR)
Root directory scanned for `org-roam` v2 nodes and `:ID:` drawers.
.TP
.B dailies_directory \fR(string, default: \fB"daily"\fR)
Subdirectory relative to `directory` storing date-stamped daily notes.
.SS [capture.templates.<name>]
Defines named note and task capture templates:
.TP
.B description \fR(string)
Human-readable summary displayed when listing capture templates.
.TP
.B target_file \fR(string)
Destination `.org` file path where captured entries are appended or filed.
.TP
.B target_heading \fR(string, optional)
Target heading title under which new entries are inserted.
.TP
.B template \fR(string)
Org heading and body template expanded during capture.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .org-tools.toml
Project configuration file at the workspace root.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
User-global fallback configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure opinionated formatting, deadline warnings, and disabled lint rules:
.PP
.nf
    [format]
    trailing_whitespace = true
    blank_lines = true
    max_consecutive_blank_lines = 1
    heading_blank_lines = true
    heading_blank_lines_before = 1
    table_format = true
    property_drawer_align = true

    [lint]
    disabled_rules = ["W001", "I003"]

    [agenda]
    deadline_warning_days = 7

    [todo]
    active = ["TODO", "NEXT", "WAITING"]
    done = ["DONE", "CANCELLED"]

    [roam]
    directory = "notes"
    dailies_directory = "daily"

    [capture.templates.inbox]
    description = "Quick inbox task"
    target_file = "inbox.org"
    target_heading = "Tasks"
    template = "* TODO %?\n:PROPERTIES:\n:CREATED: %U\n:END:\n"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B org(1)
